From dadb0820d69d40c12b2f6bfc9bc51e6117d61a56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 13:55:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] agentHost: distinguish a cancelled subscribe from a
 missing resource

A subscribe whose subscription was released while its snapshot was still
resolving got rewrapped as `Resource not found: <uri>` and logged at error
level, naming a resource that exists and was registered correctly. That made
a client-side observation lifetime problem read as a host registration bug.

Add `SubscriptionCancelledError`, a `ProtocolError` subclass thrown at every
site that already signalled `Subscription cancelled`, and key the subscribe
handler on it: the cancelled path logs at info and returns the cancellation
message rather than a missing resource. A genuinely unknown resource keeps
its code, message and error-level log.

The error reuses the session-not-found code because the synced protocol has
no cancellation code; a dedicated one would need a protocol change.
