From 58cf74cc77539525892ec523f54cabc5cec6d85b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:23:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] agentHost: keep the cancelled-subscribe log accurate
 under host disposal

`AgentService.subscribe` raises `SubscriptionCancelledError` when its store is
disposed as well as when the caller's subscription goes inactive, so naming the
client in the log made the same kind of unsupported claim this branch exists to
remove. Drop the attribution and log the neutral fact. The three handler-side
throw sites are client driven, but the one log line sees all five, so neutral
wording is the only phrasing accurate at every one of them.

Cover the reported production path at the service level too: a subscribe parked
on a pending subagent chat, cancelled before that chat materializes. The handler
test reaches that throw site through a mock, so it had no direct coverage.
---
