From 18cf909f1fe691c9ff71d8c2b9161272bcfd7526 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:53:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] agentHost: report a cancelled subscribe before an unknown
 resource

The unknown-resource check ran first, so a subscribe that was both cancelled and
whose resource never materialized still reported `Cannot subscribe to unknown
resource` at error level. The pending subagent chat path reaches that state
whenever its wait times out after the client already released the subscription,
which is the misleading message this branch exists to remove.

Test cancellation first. A live subscription is unaffected: with the caller
still active and the store not disposed the cancellation check is false and
control falls through to the same unknown-resource throw as before, so only the
cancelled-and-missing case changes.
